        answer: "You’re not buying one environment — you’re buying the factory that makes every domain after it.\n•\tWhat the premium pays for — schemas, tool framework, reward patterns, QC gates, production workflow, reviewer rubric, the playbook: one-time build.\n•\tThe curve — later domains reuse all of it: ~4–6 weeks against the first domain’s 8–10+.\n•\tTo a cheap-quote client — “A cheap one-off means domain two costs the same as domain one and you’ve bought nothing reusable. Invest a bit more now and every later domain drops.”\n•\tThe brief helps the argument — it says Food Delivery is the first of several, so the factory pays back fast.\n•\tBe honest — if they genuinely want only one domain, the calculus changes; say so.",
        answerHtml: "<strong>You’re not buying one environment — you’re buying the factory that makes every domain after it.</strong>\n•\t<strong>What the premium pays for</strong> — schemas, tool framework, reward patterns, QC gates, production workflow, reviewer rubric, the playbook: one-time build.\n•\t<strong>The curve</strong> — later domains reuse all of it: ~4–6 weeks against the first domain’s 8–10+.\n•\t<strong>To a cheap-quote client</strong> — “A cheap one-off means domain two costs the same as domain one and you’ve bought nothing reusable. Invest a bit more now and every later domain drops.”\n•\t<strong>The brief helps the argument</strong> — it says Food Delivery is the first of several, so the factory pays back fast.\n•\t<strong>Be honest</strong> — if they genuinely want only one domain, the calculus changes; say so."
